                        <fieldset id="videos">
                            <div class="form-card">
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="col-md-10">
                                        <h2 class="fs-title">
                                            Interviewer Responsibilities :
                                        </h2>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="col-md-2">
                                        <h2 class="steps">Step 2 - 8</h2>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <h5 style="margin-top:10px;font-size:21px;">Category 2 : Mandatory Interviewer Video-On Policy, Integrity & Privacy Assurance</h5>
                                <ol style="list-style: disc;font-size: 16px;">
                                    <li>
                                        Keep your camera on during the entire interview session. Keeping your video off while the interviewee has their camera on is not only unprofessional, but also unethical and disrespectful. It makes the interviewee feel like they are speaking to a faceless presence or a non-human AI agent rather than a real human expert. It creates a significant credibility gap and can raise unnecessary doubts about the interviewer’s identity, sincerity, and engagement. From the candidate's perspective, it feels like interacting with a blank screen or an AI-based agent rather than a human expert — degrading the authenticity and trust of the interview process. It gives the impression that the interviewer is not fully present or engaged, leading to discomfort, loss of confidence, and questions about the legitimacy of the process. Furthermore, allowing video-off flexibility enables fake or non-serious interviewers to conduct low-engagement interviews without being noticed. This undermines the trust and quality standards of the Risebird platform, damages its brand and reputation, and negatively impacts future business opportunities for all other hardworking and genuine interviewers.

                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Risebird is committed to upholding interviewer privacy and data protection
                                        <ol style="list-style: circle; font-size: 15px; margin: 10px;">
                                            <li>
                                                Risebird never shares resumes, emails, phone numbers, company names, or any other personal information with clients.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                All interview video recordings are automatically deleted from all records within 15 to 45 days.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Video recordings are shared only through secure URLs, accessible exclusively by authorized personnel.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Videos cannot be downloaded or screen recorded through the platform.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                In most cases, clients only browse a few minutes of the video to verify authenticity and rarely review full sessions.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>Interviewers are never matched to interview candidates from their current company.</li>
                                            <li>
                                                Interviewers are also never matched to clients that represent their current employer.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Interviewers with a consistent video-on track record will be included in Risebird's Preferred Interviewer List.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Priority for future interview allocations will be given to interviewers maintaining video-on compliance.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Risebird plans to discontinue assigning interviews to interviewers who do not keep their camera on during interviews in the coming weeks.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                In the rarest of rare cases where interviewers face concerns or issues with video-on participation, they are encouraged to clarify that a video conversation alone does not constitute any employment or part-time work association with Risebird or its clients. Proof of monetary transaction is a prerequisite for any professional engagement acknowledgement.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                Additionally, conducting video interviews on Risebird can enhance your visibility as a professional. Many clients, upon seeing an impressive interview recording, may express interest in hiring the interviewer for full-time roles.
                                            </li>
                                            <li>
                                                In this sense, video interviews on Risebird function similarly to publishing professional content on LinkedIn — creating passive opportunities for employment through visible expertise.
                                            </li>
                                        </ol>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Conduct interviews personally without any impersonation or delegation.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Do not engage in multitasking or unrelated activities during the interview.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Maintain full attention and active engagement throughout the interview duration.
                                    </li>
                                </ol>

