                                        Align all questions with the designated scoring rubric, ensuring they reflect the expected depth, topic areas, and outcomes.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Tailor questions to match the seniority level, job description (JD), client expectations, and interview flow.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Avoid mismatched questions — for example, asking a basic coding problem to an architect-level candidate.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Focus on evaluating actual hands-on skills and applied talent rather than relying on theoretical or memorized knowledge.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Focus on evaluating actual hands-on skills and applied talent rather than relying on theoretical or memorized knowledge.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Design questions that are insightful, discerning, and capable of evaluating real-time thinking.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Avoid questions that can be easily answered using generative AI tools or by memorizing theoretical material.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>Maintain at least 80% original content in questions to avoid plagiarism.</li>
                                    <li>
                                        Clearly disclose the use of AI-generated content or assistance if applicable.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Regularly refine and update questions to reflect current industry standards and client feedback.
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        Avoid repetitive, abstract, or irrelevant questions that detract from accurate candidate assessment.
                                    </li>
                                </ol>

